# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bus Sun-Side Advisor — environment variables
#
# There is nothing you have to set. No API key, no billing account, no sign-up:
# the app runs on OpenStreetMap's public services out of the box. Copy this file
# only if you want to override one of the defaults below:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored by the Next.js default .gitignore.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OPTIONAL. Routing engine (OSRM) used for the route, its alternatives, the
# distance, the duration and the step timings.
#
# The default is the OSRM demo server, which is free but explicitly *not* meant
# for production traffic: it is rate-limited, occasionally slow, and offers no
# uptime guarantee. Point this at your own OSRM instance for anything serious.
#
#   OSRM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000
#
# Default: https://router.project-osrm.org
#OSRM_BASE_URL=

# OPTIONAL. Geocoder (Nominatim), used only when a pasted link carries a place
# name or an OSM object id instead of coordinates.
#
# The default is OpenStreetMap's public Nominatim, whose usage policy caps you
# at roughly one request per second and forbids bulk use. Self-host or use a
# commercial endpoint if you expect real traffic.
#
# Default: https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org
#NOMINATIM_BASE_URL=

# OPTIONAL. The User-Agent sent to OSRM and Nominatim.
#
# This is not cosmetic: Nominatim answers 403 to requests that do not identify
# the application making them. Set it to something that names your deployment
# and gives a contact address, e.g.
#
#   OSM_USER_AGENT=BusSunAdvisor/1.0 (you@example.com)
#
# Default: a generic BusSunAdvisor/1.0 string.
#OSM_USER_AGENT=

# OPTIONAL. Tile source for the route preview.
#
# This one *does* carry the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, deliberately: the browser
# fetches the tiles directly, so the value has to reach the client. There is no
# secret involved — it is a public tile URL either way.
#
# If you change it, keep the attribution the map displays accurate: OpenStreetMap's
# tile policy requires crediting the data, and other providers have their own terms.
#
# Default: https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
#NEXT_PUBLIC_TILE_URL_TEMPLATE=
